                ],
                [
                    603.0,
                    673.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    673.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "• At  $ \\lambda_{ortho} = 0.0 $ (Fig. 9a), the embeddings form loosely structured clusters in the latent feature space, with considerable overlap between semantically similar parts (e.g., Dorsal and Adipose Fins). Such poor separability in the embedding space leads to ambiguous representations and reduces segmentation precision.",
            "block_bbox": [
                113,
                678,
                602,
                820
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    113.0,
                    678.0
                ],
                [
                    602.0,
                    678.0
                ],
                [
                    602.0,
                    820.0
                ],
                [
                    113.0,
                    820.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "• At  $ \\lambda_{ortho} = 0.5 $ (Fig. 9b), the embeddings form more compact and well-separated clusters in the latent feature space. The prototype vectors ( $ \\star $ markers) align with the centers of their corresponding semantic clusters, encouraging intra-class cohesion while improving inter-class separability.",
            "block_bbox": [
                112,
                823,
                603,
                964
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    112.0,
                    823.0
                ],
                [
                    603.0,
                    823.0
                ],
                [
                    603.0,
                    964.0
                ],
                [
                    112.0,
                    964.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "• At  $ \\lambda_{ortho} = 1.0 $ (Fig. 9c), the embeddings form highly compact clusters with strong inter-class separation in the latent space. However, this overly rigid structure (Separation Score: 58.96) may reduce the model's ability to capture intra-class variations in unseen species, leading to a slight drop in OOD performance as discussed in Section V. In practice,  $ \\lambda_{ortho} = 0.5 $ provides the best trade-off between discriminability and generalization.",
            "block_bbox": [
                111,
                966,
                603,
                1158
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    111.0,
                    966.0
                ],
                [
                    603.0,
                    966.0
                ],
                [
                    603.0,
                    1158.0
                ],
                [
                    111.0,
                    1158.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Prototype correlation analysis: Fig. 10 displays the cosine similarity matrix between learned prototypes at  $ \\lambda_{ortho} = 0.5 $. Ideally, prototypes representing distinct anatomical parts should be orthogonal (correlation  $ \\approx 0 $). The heatmap shows low correlation values (< 0.2) for most pairs, confirming that FISHER successfully learns distinct representations for different body parts. Notably, even for spatially adjacent and visually similar parts such as the Anal and Pelvic Fins, the correlation remains low, highlighting the effectiveness of the proposed attribute-aware learning objective. A slight positive correlation exists between Adipose and Barbel (0.67), likely due to their shared property as small, high-frequency texture features, yet they remain sufficiently distinct for accurate segmentation.",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                1164,
                604,
                1500
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
